STEP 3 — DOCUMENT VALIDATION RULES

Inspect the actual application and "PandemicJS.js" to establish the rules below.

A. District E-Pass

Document and test these known requirements:

- Name: mandatory, non-empty text; no letters-only restriction is enforced.
- Email: mandatory, non-empty text; email format is not validated.
- Mobile Number: three separate segments; each segment must be non-empty, with maximum lengths of 3, 3, and 4 characters respectively. Numeric-only enforcement is not applied.
- District: a selection other than the default "------Select------" is required.
- Gender: one radio option among Male, Female, and Others must be selected.
- Aadhaar Number: mandatory, non-empty text; length and digit format are not validated.
- Reason: a selection other than the default "------Select------" is required.
- All seven fields are mandatory.

B. State E-Pass

Document and test these known requirements:

- Name: mandatory, non-empty text.
- Email: mandatory, non-empty text; email format is not validated.
- Mobile Number: three separate non-empty segments, with maximum lengths of 3, 3, and 4 characters. Numeric-only enforcement is not applied.
- State: a selection other than the default "------Select------" is required.
- Gender: one radio option among Male, Female, and Others must be selected.
- Aadhaar Number: mandatory, non-empty text; length and digit format are not validated.
- Reason: a selection other than the default "------Select------" is required.
- Travel By: a selection other than the default "------Select------" is required.
- Travel Date: mandatory, non-empty text; date format is not validated.
- Anything to Say: optional textarea.
